{
  "title": "SequenceContext",
  "description": "What a running step can do: wait on the sequencer's clock, wait for signals, conditions, handles and operations, and start branches. Each step has its own context. Every wait is a generator, used with `yield*`; its result is the value of the `yield*` expression. A step that waits resumes inside a later tick of the sequencer, in the frame phase the sequencer runs in, never in a promise continuation.",
  "symbol": "SequenceContext",
